cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VEXPACE in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "VEXPACE: An Open-Source Particle-in-Cell Simulation Framework for Plasma and Vacuum Electronics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Faisal"
    given-names: "Md Arifuzzaman"
    affiliation: "Department of Nuclear Engineering and Radiological Sciences, University of Michigan"
abstract: >-
  VEXPACE is a Python particle-in-cell code for space-charge-limited flow, electron beams, plasmas and
  vacuum electron devices in 1D-Z, 2D-ZY and 2D-RZ geometry, with finite-element electrostatic and Yee
  FDTD electromagnetic solvers, a model-builder graphical interface, a command-line runner and a Python API.
